Upstream: none found.

When the end of a chained physical stream is bisected, the bisection can end with the end bound
inside the last page of the stream. Reading that page from the start bound leaves the reader past
the end bound, so byte_range_end - pos in scan_stream_end underflows (a panic with overflow checks,
a huge scope length without them). Without overflow checks, a page with a bad CRC that follows
then makes the page reader seek within the ScopedStream, whose end wraps, and clamp() panics with
min > max. The test builds such a stream.

